{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Frontend Route & Navigation Guard",
  "description": "Monitors React Router files and route components to verify route integrity, validate imports, check navigation links, and ensure proper error state handling when routes are modified",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/routes/**/*.js",
      "**/routes/**/*.jsx",
      "**/routes/**/*.ts",
      "**/routes/**/*.tsx",
      "**/src/App.js",
      "**/src/App.jsx",
      "**/src/App.ts",
      "**/src/App.tsx",
      "**/pages/**/*.js",
      "**/pages/**/*.jsx",
      "**/pages/**/*.ts",
      "**/pages/**/*.tsx",
      "**/*Router*.js",
      "**/*Router*.jsx",
      "**/*Router*.ts",
      "**/*Router*.tsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A frontend route or navigation file has been modified. Please:\n\n1. **Route Definition Analysis**: Examine the changed route files to detect:\n   - New, modified, or removed route definitions\n   - Changes to route parameters, paths, or components\n   - Lazy-loaded route imports and component references\n\n2. **Route Integrity Validation**: Verify that:\n   - All route component imports are valid and resolve correctly\n   - Lazy-loaded components exist and can be imported\n   - Route paths don't conflict or create ambiguous matches\n   - Route parameters are properly defined and used\n\n3. **Navigation Link Audit**: Check for:\n   - Navigation links that may now point to invalid routes\n   - Redirect configurations that need updating\n   - Breadcrumb or menu items that reference changed routes\n   - Deep links and bookmarkable URLs that still work\n\n4. **Error State Verification**: Ensure:\n   - 404/Not Found pages render correctly for invalid routes\n   - Unauthorized/403 pages work for protected routes\n   - Empty states display properly when no data is available\n   - Loading states show during route transitions\n\n5. **Test Generation/Updates**: \n   - Generate or update route-level smoke tests\n   - Create Playwright/Cypress navigation tests if testing framework is present\n   - Add tests for new routes or update tests for modified routes\n   - Include tests for error states and edge cases\n\n6. **Route Performance Check**: Verify:\n   - Code splitting is working for lazy routes\n   - Bundle sizes haven't increased significantly\n   - Route preloading is configured appropriately\n\nPlease run any existing tests and create new ones as needed to ensure the routing changes don't break the application's navigation flow."
  }
}